<title>BRAZIL: Injunction won't delay Cemig sale - state.</title>
<headline>Injunction won't delay Cemig sale - state.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>An injunction granted to halt the May 6 sale of a 32.9 percent stake in Brazilian state-owned Cemig will be appealed and is unlikely to delay the auction, a state spokesman said.</p>
<p>&quot;The state will appeal. So far, there has been no change in the auction date,&quot; said Alvaro Cunha, a spokesman for Minas Gerais Finance Secretary.</p>
<p>Cunha said injunction, which halts the sale of debentures convertible to voting shares, would be lifted automatically as soon as the state appeals the ruling.</p>
<p>Late on Friday, a local judge granted an injuction sought by a lawyer representing a group of Minas Gerais state residents opposed to the sale.</p>
<p>The injunction prompted speculation that long-awaited sale would be delayed again.</p>
<p>((-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5415))</p>
